  "request": {
    "spec": "When a person is edited, the form remembers which version of the person it loaded. If someone\nelse has saved that person in the meantime, saving is refused with an error on the form, nothing\nis stored, and the form shows the current values; opening the editor again and saving works.\nSubmitting any form twice before the first submit has answered stores one record, not two.\n",
    "prompt": "You are implementing ONE change to this application.\n\nFIRST read AGENTS.md \u2014 it states the working rules and how the app is tested, and sends you to\nDESIGN.md for the app's stack and conventions. Follow both.\n\nTHE CHANGE REQUEST:\nWhen a person is edited, the form remembers which version of the person it loaded. If someone\nelse has saved that person in the meantime, saving is refused with an error on the form, nothing\nis stored, and the form shows the current values; opening the editor again and saving works.\nSubmitting any form twice before the first submit has answered stores one record, not two.\n\nYour work is verified by an automated Playwright UI test already installed under e2e/specs/.\nRead that spec: it declares the exact data-testid anchors, values, test data and any audit\nrecords it expects \u2014 match them. Run `bin/e2e` to build the app, start it, and run the test as\nyou work; iterate until it passes. Change whatever the request needs across the app \u2014 its stored\ndata, its server and its front end. Do NOT edit bin/build, bin/start, bin/stop, bin/e2e,\nAGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, DESIGN.md, e2e/support/ or the test spec.\n"
  },
